---
import {stops,locations,stopURL} from '../lib/catalog';
const placed=locations.filter(l=>l.coordinates!==null);
const x=(lon:number)=>80+(lon+93.102)*40000*Math.cos(44.94*Math.PI/180);
const y=(lat:number)=>60+(44.947-lat)*40000;
---
<figure class="geographic-preview">
 <svg viewBox="0 0 1000 650" role="img" aria-labelledby="map-title map-desc"><title id="map-title">Three approximate venue positions in Saint Paul</title><desc id="map-desc">North is up. The hotel and Landmark Center are close together northwest of the caves. Four other stops remain unplaced. This coordinate grid has no river or street base layer yet. Use the directory below for links and full qualifications.</desc>
 <rect x="0" y="0" width="1000" height="650" fill="#151A24"/>
 {[44.935,44.94,44.945].map(lat=><g><line x1="70" x2="640" y1={y(lat)} y2={y(lat)} stroke="#63718a" stroke-dasharray="4 5"/><text x="10" y={y(lat)-7} fill="#B8B8BC" font-size="16">{lat}°N</text></g>)}
 {[-93.1,-93.095,-93.09,-93.085].map(lon=><g><line y1="45" y2="580" x1={x(lon)} x2={x(lon)} stroke="#63718a" stroke-dasharray="4 5"/><text x={x(lon)} y="610" fill="#B8B8BC" font-size="16" text-anchor="middle">{Math.abs(lon)}°W</text></g>)}
 <text x="925" y="50" fill="#F3EFE6" font-size="22">N ↑</text>
 {placed.map((l,i)=>{const stop=stops.find(s=>s.locationId===l.id)!;const labelY=110+i*125;return <g><circle cx={x(l.coordinates!.longitude)} cy={y(l.coordinates!.latitude)} r="20" fill="none" stroke="#FF8293" stroke-width="3" stroke-dasharray="5 4"/><text x={x(l.coordinates!.longitude)} y={y(l.coordinates!.latitude)+6} text-anchor="middle" fill="#F3EFE6" font-size="18">{stop.order}</text><path d={`M${x(l.coordinates!.longitude)+22},${y(l.coordinates!.latitude)} L660,${labelY}`} fill="none" stroke="#B8B8BC"/><text x="675" y={labelY} fill="#F3EFE6" font-size="19">{stop.order}. {l.currentName}</text><text x="675" y={labelY+25} fill="#FF8293" font-size="17">Approximate venue area</text></g>;})}
 </svg><figcaption>North-up coordinate sketch. Dashed outlines indicate uncertain venue areas, not measured boundaries. No event footprints or travel connections are asserted. Coordinate sources and dates appear below; the finished river/base layer remains under review.</figcaption>
</figure>
<section><h2>The seven-stop directory</h2><p>Every chapter can be read at home. Three venue positions are shown approximately from published geographic records. Four chapters remain unplaced. An address does not establish an exact historical event footprint.</p>
 <ol class="location-list">{stops.map(s=>{const l=locations.find(l=>l.id===s.locationId);if(!l)return null;return <li id={`location-${l.id}`} class="card"><p class="eyebrow">Stop {s.order} · {l.role}</p><h3><a href={stopURL(s.id)}>{s.title}</a></h3><p><strong>{l.historicalName}</strong><br/>{l.address}</p><p>{s.synopsis}</p><p>Position: <strong>{l.precision}</strong> · Condition: <strong>{l.condition}</strong> · Access: <strong>{l.access}</strong></p><p>{l.qualification}</p>{l.coordinates&&<p class="muted"><a href={l.coordinates.sourceUrl}>Coordinate source</a>, checked {l.coordinates.checkedDate}. {l.coordinates.method} Structured Wikimedia place coordinates are available under CC0; no source photograph is reproduced.</p>}{l.currentCheck&&<p class="muted">Address/access note checked {l.currentCheck.date}: {l.currentCheck.note} <a href={l.currentCheck.url}>Current venue source</a></p>}<p><a href={`/sources/#source-${l.supportingSourceId}`}>Historical source {l.supportingSourceId}</a> — {l.supportingLocator}</p><p class="muted" data-visited-stop={s.id} data-js-control hidden></p></li>})}</ol>
</section>

<style>.geographic-preview{margin-block:2rem}.geographic-preview svg{width:100%}@media(max-width:600px){.geographic-preview svg{display:none}}</style>
